From: Dominique Leuenberger <dimstar@opensuse.org>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] include/linux/bvec.h: alias bi_bvec_done and bi_offset in struct bvec_iter
Upstream: pending

In Linux 7.3+, the kernel block layer renamed bi_bvec_done to bi_offset
in struct bvec_iter.
When building against kernel headers >= 7.3, kernel-synced code like
fs/data/read.c checks LINUX_VERSION_CODE and attempts to access
bi_iter.bi_offset.
However, bcachefs-tools compiles against its own bundled userspace
include/linux/bvec.h header which still had bi_bvec_done.

Use an anonymous union in struct bvec_iter to alias bi_bvec_done and
bi_offset, satisfying both modern kernel-synced code and existing
userspace iterator helpers without macro pollution.

---
 include/linux/bvec.h | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/include/linux/bvec.h
+++ b/include/linux/bvec.h
@@ -38,8 +38,10 @@ struct bvec_iter {
 
 	unsigned int		bi_idx;		/* current index into bvl_vec */
 
-	unsigned int            bi_bvec_done;	/* number of bytes completed in
-						   current bvec */
+	union {
+		unsigned int    bi_bvec_done;	/* number of bytes completed in current bvec */
+		unsigned int    bi_offset;
+	};
 };
 
 struct bvec_iter_all {
